    "result_text": "All 282 tests pass, including the new Cp17 test. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` flag on owner creation. When a `POST /api/owners` creates an owner, the response's `sharesHousehold` is `true` if another owner already had the same address and city, otherwise `false`; creation is always allowed.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `sharesHousehold` (`Boolean`, column `shares_household`) field with getter/setter, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads it back like `namesakeCount`.\n\n2. **Schema SQL** (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `shares_household` column to the `owners` table.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n4. **`AssignSharesHousehold.java`** \u2014 new OfficeFloor function that scans existing owners and sets the flag `true` when another owner matches on both address and city (case- and whitespace-insensitive, using the existing `DuplicateMatching`, consistent with the other owner rules). The owner isn't saved yet, so it never matches itself.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline after `assignNamesakeCount` and before `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe new `Cp17Tests` passes (first owner at an address \u2192 `false`, second at the same address+city \u2192 `true`), and the full suite (282 tests) is green.",
